    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d603">

                <pb facs="0686" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.6363/775: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-13T00:00:00+01:00">April 13,
                            1943—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received April 14—8:23 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>897. My 872 [<hi rendition="#italic">822</hi>], April 6, 4 p.m. War Department
                    has informed Military Attaché Joint General Staffs have recommended aviation <pb
                        facs="0687" n="675" xml:id="pg675"/> gasoline be supplied to Spain in amount
                    of 420 tons per month. British Ambassador has received similar telegram from
                    London and has requested details as well as authorization to communicate
                    decision to Spaniards when he and I agree conditions are propitious. I concur
                    and request similar authorization as well as details.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
